2. Known problems                                                                                 
                                                                                                  
   2.1  When the segment of resistor is larger than one, the simulation values could not be       
        back-annotated to schematic view correctly.                                               
                                                                                                  
   2.2 	NMOS with DNW must be surrounded with NWELL.
   
   2.3 The minimum RPO area of resistors should be checked. 
   
   2.4 In some special length and width ranges of resistors, their resistance values shown in CDF menu have
       differences compared with simulation results. These resistance values are for reference only, and 
       users should run simulations to get correct results.        

3. Special Notes

   3.1 If polyroute direction is not set to "none", and  the finger number should be more than 2.

   3.2 The mosfets with macro model ("_mac") and normal mosfets can not be used in schematic simultaneously
       for LVS/RCX. Users need to turn on/off MACRO switch in LVS/RCX deck by themselves. 

   3.3 MOS with DNW must be surrounded with NWELL.

   3.4 Please read all PDK documents in /PDK_Doc/ carefully before using this PDK.         
   
   3.5 source.added will be added automatically in Assura Netlist File(s) and Calibre Netlist Export Setup.
   
   3.6 The "About this PDK tool utility" will pop-up automatically when invoking virtuoso. Please read the ReleaseNote
       and REVISION carefully before using this PDK.
   
   3.7 The designs with PDK, T-018-CM-SP-007-K3 are not compatible with those of T-018-MM-SP-001 and T-018-MM-SP-002 
       because of model and netlist behavior inconsistence. The design with T-018-MM-SP-00-K3 can not be plugged 
       in T-018-CM-SP-007-K3, either. Users need to create new designs by themselves. 
       
   3.8 The capacitance value shown in crtmom CDF menu is Cab+Cap, not only Cab.
   
   3.9 All the cells included in this PDK are built based on current design rule documents and spice model cards. Some of rules or parameters may be changed after this release, please contact TSMC for the most up-to-date information.   
   
   3.10 Please do not use the devices in "do_not_use" category.   

   3.11 MOS with WPE effect:
 	    1) WPE effect: Netlist generated from PDK contains SCA,SCB,SCC parameters for 
 	        Bsim4.5 simulation. For pre-simulation, users can modify these parameters in 
 	        MOS CDF form if they are available. For post-simulation, LPE tools will extract
 	        SCA,SCB,SCC from layout.
 	        
 	    * Since there is no implant on native devices, there will be no WPE effect on those devices. 
 	      But there are still SCA,SCB,SCC parameters in the model of native device. 
   
